pastex (2.32.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Select button is an icon button again. Entering select mode wrote
    "Select" and "Done" into it, overwriting the glyph with a word, which broke
    the one rule every other button follows; the glyph now stays, and the
    pressed style and the tooltip (Select items to move or delete / Leave select
    mode) carry the state.
  * Fixed: the in-page launcher kept offering to close a panel that was already
    closed. Closing the panel from the extension icon or from Chrome's own panel
    switch runs no code in the panel, so nothing told the page and the button
    stayed on x. The worker now follows sidePanel.onOpened / onClosed, which
    Chrome fires for every way a panel closes, and every authorization the page
    asks for carries the current state, so the button recovers even after a
    missed message. The minimum browser version is therefore Chrome/Chromium 142.
  * Fixed: Sync was expensive. Sending the queue was followed by a full read of
    the library, so syncing two snippets downloaded every snippet the user owns.
    Sending a change does not change the shape of the library, only the ids of
    the rows it creates, so those ids are adopted in place and the read is
    skipped. A browser start still touches Drive only when the queue is not
    empty, and only a real change (a queued write, another configuration, or the
    idle check finding a difference) asks Drive again.

