pastex (2.28.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING: the requested scope is now `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive`
    — the full Drive scope, one scope and nothing else. Pastex asks Google for
    complete access to the signed-in account's Drive, with no narrowing of its
    own, and the library folder in the configuration stops being a limit on what
    the token can reach and becomes only what Pastex chooses to read and write.
  * This is what makes the existing installations readable again: `drive.file`
    reaches only the files Pastex created or the user opened through it, so a
    folder made by hand in Drive, a snippet uploaded from a phone, or a file
    copied into the library folder answered HTTP 404 as if it did not exist.
    Those files are all readable now, and files added to the library folder from
    outside Pastex appear in the panel like any other snippet.
  * The consequence is stated plainly in the README and in SECURITY.md: the
    scope is classified as restricted by Google, so while the consent screen
    stays in Testing with you as a test user it works without review, but
    publishing it for other people requires a security assessment.
  * Because the scope changed, the grant Google holds no longer matches: accept
    the sign-in once after the upgrade, and every later read is silent again.
  * The "cannot see the library folder" message became "cannot open the library
    folder": with the full scope a 404/403 is about the folder — a wrong id, a
    deleted folder, or an account that never had it shared — not about the grant
    being too narrow.

