pastex (2.27.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING: the requested scope is `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file`
    again, and the grant has to be approved once more. `drive.item` is not in
    Google's scope tables — not among the non-sensitive scopes, the sensitive
    ones or the restricted ones — so Google refused the request with
    `invalid_scope` and no token was issued. `drive.file` is the per-file scope
    Google publishes: it reaches the files Pastex creates and the files the
    configuration links name, and nothing else in Drive. The account-wide
    `drive` scope is still not requested.
  * Because the requested scope changed, the grant Google already holds no
    longer matches: the next read asks for approval once, and every later read
    is silent again.
  * The guide in the extension README now names `auth/drive.file` and says
    plainly why `auth/drive.item` must not be substituted for it.

