pastex (2.23.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING: Drive access now runs as you, through Google OAuth, and the
    service account is gone. Pastex asks Chrome to open Google's sign-in page
    for a client id you create once, and keeps only an access token in memory
    for about an hour. The files it writes belong to your Google account, count
    against your own Drive storage, and open normally in Drive. The whole class
    of "a folder can be created but a snippet cannot" disappears with it: a
    service account has no storage of its own, so Google refused every file it
    tried to create in a personal folder.
  * BREAKING: configuration is three files, and the key file is no longer one
    of them. `service-account.json` is replaced by `pastex-oauth.json`, which
    holds only the public client id of your installation (for example
    `{"client_id": "123456789012-abcdefghijklmnop.apps.googleusercontent.com"}`).
    All three files (`pastex-google-drive.json`, `pastex-sites.json`,
    `pastex-oauth.json`) must now carry their exact names; the old rule that
    recognised a key by its content is removed with the key. The cached
    configuration shape moved to version 3, so Pastex asks for the folder once
    more after the upgrade.
  * No client secret is needed, and none is accepted: an extension is a public
    client, and Google hands the token back to Chrome directly. Only the
    `drive.file` scope is requested, which reaches the files Pastex itself
    created and nothing else. Signing out revokes the token at Google.
  * The sign-in window reports the exact redirect URL to register
    (`https://<extension-id>.chromiumapp.org/`) when Google answers
    `redirect_uri_mismatch`, and a 401 drops the cached token and retries once
    instead of leaving the queue stuck until the browser restarts.
  * The extension README now carries the complete OAuth guide: Cloud project,
    Drive API, consent screen, client creation, publishing, and the client id
    file. The manifest gains the `identity` permission.
  * BREAKING: `scripts/check-drive-write.sh` and
    `scripts/get-pastex-label.sh` are removed. Both existed only to sign in a
    service account with `openssl`, and the project does not keep two ways to
    do one thing. `where-order-and-collapse-live.md` keeps the two API calls
    that read the index, which now run as the signed-in account.

