pastex (2.21.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: a reorder or a fold could never be saved. The index was stored as a
    custom property on the root folder, and Drive limits a property to 124 bytes
    including its key name; the key alone is 12 of those, so two rows already
    overflowed it and Drive answered HTTP 400. The panel kept the change in its
    own cache and eventually reported it as "refused". This is why order and
    collapse looked broken while creating a folder worked.
  * BREAKING: the index moved to one small file in the library folder,
    pastex-index.json. The old folder property is not read any more; a library
    ordered with 2.20 or earlier falls back to Drive's order with every folder
    open until the next reorder or fold writes the file. Snippet files are
    untouched and pastex-index.json is never shown as a snippet.
  * The Sync button now reports a refused write with Drive's own message
    instead of a smaller count, so a permanent refusal is visible immediately.
  * New: scripts/check-drive-write.sh writes one folder, one snippet and one
    index file into the library and prints Drive's exact answer for each. It
    tells a permission or quota problem apart from a Pastex problem and removes
    what it created. This answers the case where a folder can be created but a
    snippet cannot.

