pastex (2.16.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remove every layer the product no longer runs. A module that no page or
    worker loads is a second implementation that drifts, so it is gone rather
    than kept "just in case":
      - handle-store.js (IndexedDB folder handle) and config-import.js
        (folder-file discovery) were left over from the folder-handle design;
        the panel scans the folder directly and stores the parsed JSON.
      - config-source.js no longer takes unused store/discovery arguments, and
        its write-only exports describe(), clearCache(), invalidate() and
        readCached() are removed. create(sites, cacheStore) is the whole API.
      - drive.js no longer exports the per-item writers setOrder/setCollapsed.
        Reorder and fold have written the single pastex_index label since
        2.12; a second writer for the same fact is a second source of truth.
        The per-item labels are still read for libraries written by older
        versions.
      - store.js loses flatten(), findById() and search(); the panel uses
        createIndex(), which returns the same lookups precomputed.
      - library.js stops exporting loadTree, parseIndex, nodeSignature and
        emptyIndex; cache.js stops exporting pending and invalidate; the
        config cache reader stops exporting hasConfiguration; drive.js stops
        exporting DRIVE_URL, SCOPES, bytesToBase64Url and pemToPkcs8.
  * No behaviour changes: this release only deletes code that was unreachable
    from sidepanel.html, the manifest and the worker.
  * New extension/test/dead-code.test.js fails the build when a shipped file
    is not reachable, when sidepanel.html loads a module that does not provide
    a Pastex* global the panel uses, or when the per-item Drive writers come
    back.
  * ARCHITECTURE.md explains the project to a reader who does not program.

