pastex (2.15.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed "Could not read the library: The request is not allowed by the user
    agent or the platform in the current context." The background worker asked
    an offscreen document for configuration, and that document tried to use the
    user's folder handle. File System Access handles are not usable there.
  * Configuration is now read once from the folder and cached. The panel scans
    the chosen folder when it is picked, stores the parsed JSON in
    chrome.storage.local, and both the panel and the worker read that cache.
    The folder is a source of configuration, never its storage: later reads do
    not open it at all, so a browser restart needs no folder grant.
  * Only the surface of the folder is scanned. Subfolders are skipped without
    being entered, non-.json files are ignored, and JSON that does not parse is
    skipped instead of failing the whole folder.
  * Removed the offscreen configuration reader (config-reader.html/.js and
    config-client.js). The worker imports config-cache-reader.js instead, so
    "offscreen" is no longer needed for configuration.
  * Re-selecting a folder no longer wipes the cached configuration: the worker
    keeps what the panel just wrote and only resets the library and queue.
  * Status messages under the buttons are shorter and plainer.
  * Fixed two storage bugs found while porting: chrome.storage.get() resolves
    to an object keyed by the requested name, but both readers treated that
    wrapper as the record, so `files` was undefined on every later open.

